[size=6][b]Event-PVP-Plugin - Quick Description[/b][/size]

A comprehensive Minecraft plugin that combines [b]custom event management[/b] and [b]PvP wager system[/b] into one unified solution.

[b]🌍 Multilingual Support: Available in 8 Languages[/b] (English, German, French, Spanish, Russian, Polish, Japanese, Chinese)

[size=5][b]What Does This Plugin Do?[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Event System[/b][/size]
Host custom server events with:
[list]
[*]Multiple event types (PvP Arena, Capture the Flag, Free-for-All, etc.)
[*]Automated event scheduling
[*]Configurable spawn systems (single point, random, team-based)
[*]Custom rewards for winners and participants
[*]Statistics tracking and leaderboards
[/list]

[size=4][b]PvP Wager System[/b][/size]
Let players bet on PvP matches:
[list]
[*]Challenge other players with item or money wagers
[*]Multiple arena configurations
[*]Pre-configured equipment sets
[*]Spectator mode for watching matches
[*]Match management (draw votes, surrender, timeouts)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Web Interface[/b][/size]
Configure everything through a modern browser interface:
[list]
[*]Edit all YAML configurations visually
[*]Create events and equipment sets with live preview
[*]Token-based secure access
[*][b]Multi-language support: 8 languages[/b] (EN, DE, FR, ES, RU, PL, JA, ZH)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Important Dependencies[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]⚠️ Multiverse-Core (REQUIRED)[/b][/size]
[b]This plugin fundamentally requires Multiverse-Core[/b] for proper operation:
[list]
[*][b]World Loading[/b]: Loads event/arena worlds when matches start
[*][b]World Cloning[/b]: Creates temporary world copies from templates
[*][b]World Regeneration[/b]: Resets worlds after events/matches
[*][b]World Unloading[/b]: Unloads worlds to save server resources
[/list]

[b]Without Multiverse-Core[/b], the plugin will have limited functionality and may not work correctly.

[size=4][b]⚠️ Multiverse-Inventories (STRONGLY RECOMMENDED)[/b][/size]
[b]Multiverse-Inventories is essential for proper inventory restoration[/b]. Here's why:

[b]The Problem:[/b]
[list]
[*]When players join an event or PvP match, they are teleported to a different world
[*]Their inventory is cleared and replaced with event/match equipment
[*]When returning to the main world, they need their original inventory back
[/list]

[b]The Solution:[/b]
Multiverse-Inventories handles this automatically:
[list]
[*][b]Separate Inventories[/b]: Each world group (main, event, pvp) has its own inventory
[*][b]Automatic Switching[/b]: When players change worlds, their inventory is automatically restored
[*][b]No Data Loss[/b]: Player inventories are preserved by Multiverse-Inventories
[/list]

[b]Without Multiverse-Inventories:[/b]
[list]
[*]The plugin has a fallback inventory backup system, but it's still [b]experimental and buggy[/b]
[*]Players may lose items or experience inventory issues
[*]Inventory restoration is not guaranteed to work correctly
[/list]

[b]Recommended Setup:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install Multiverse-Core
[*]Install Multiverse-Inventories
[*]Configure world groups in Multiverse-Inventories:
[list]
[*][font=courier new]default[/font] group: Main/survival worlds
[*][font=courier new]event[/font] group: Event worlds
[*][font=courier new]pvp[/font] group: PvP arena worlds
[/list]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Other Dependencies[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Vault[/b] (Required): For economy integration (money wagers)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Essential Commands[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]For Players[/b][/size]

[b]Events:[/b]
[code]
/event <name> join          - Join an event
/event <name> leave         - Leave an event
/event list                 - Show available events
/eventstats me              - View your event statistics
[/code]

[b]PvP Wagers:[/b]
[code]
/pvpask <player>                                      - Challenge a player (GUI)
/pvpa <player> <wager> <amount> <arena> <equipment>  - Challenge with full setup
/pvpaccept [player]                                   - Accept a challenge
/pvpdeny [player]                                     - Deny a challenge
/surrender                                            - Surrender current match
/draw                                                 - Vote for a draw
/pvp spectate <player>                                - Spectate a match
/pvpstats me                                          - View your PvP statistics
[/code]

[b]Examples:[/b]
[code]
/pvpa Steve DIAMOND_SWORD 1 PvPArena diamond_pvp    - Challenge Steve with item wager
/pvpa Alex MONEY 100 desert standard                - Challenge Alex with $100 wager
/pvpa Mike SKIP 0 forest pvp_starter                - Challenge Mike without wager
[/code]

[size=4][b]For Admins[/b][/size]

[code]
/eventpvp reload            - Reload all configurations
/eventpvp webtoken          - Generate web interface access token
/event <name> start         - Start an event
/event <name> stop          - Stop an event
/event <name> forcestart    - Force start without minimum players
/pvpadmin reload            - Reload PvP configuration
/pvpadmin stopall           - Stop all active matches
/inventoryrestore <player> <ID>  - Restore player inventory (fallback)
[/code]

[size=5][b]Quick Start[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*][b]Install Dependencies:[/b]
[list]
[*]Vault
[*]Multiverse-Core
[*]Multiverse-Inventories
[/list]

[*][b]Configure World Groups[/b] (in Multiverse-Inventories):
[code]
/mvinv group default
/mvinv group event
/mvinv group pvp
[/code]

[*][b]Assign Worlds to Groups:[/b]
[code]
/mvinv world <world_name> event
/mvinv world <arena_name> pvp
[/code]

[*][b]Configure the Plugin:[/b]
[list]
[*]Edit [font=courier new]config.yml[/font], [font=courier new]worlds.yml[/font], [font=courier new]equipment.yml[/font]
[*]Or use the web interface: [font=courier new]/eventpvp webtoken[/font]
[/list]

[*][b]Reload and Test:[/b]
[code]
/eventpvp reload
/event pvparena start
[/code]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Server Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Platform[/b]: Paper/Spigot 1.19+
[*][b]RAM[/b]: 4GB+ recommended (depending on world size)
[*][b]Multiverse-Core[/b]: Latest version
[*][b]Multiverse-Inventories[/b]: Latest version (strongly recommended)
[*][b]Vault[/b]: Latest version
[/list]

[size=5][b]Need Help?[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Check the full [font=courier new]README.md[/font] for detailed documentation
[*]Review configuration examples in [font=courier new]CONFIG_EXAMPLES.md[/font]
[*]Test spawn configurations using [font=courier new]SpawnExamples.md[/font]
[/list]

[hr]

[b]Remember[/b]: Multiverse-Core and Multiverse-Inventories are not just optional - they are [b]essential[/b] for this plugin to work properly!
